// Reset a half-open connection, then open another with the same client ISN.
// The new server ISN is learned even though the client SYN sequence repeats.
// Its duplicate SYN must still get the same SYN-ACK ISN.
// expect-pass

0     < S 0:0(0) win 64240 <mss 1460,sackOK,eol,eol>
+0    > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,sackOK,eol,eol>
+0    < R 1:1(0) win 0

+0.1  < S 0:0(0) win 64240 <mss 1460,sackOK,eol,eol>
+0    > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,sackOK,eol,eol>
+0.1  < S 0:0(0) win 64240 <mss 1460,sackOK,eol,eol>
+0    > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,sackOK,eol,eol>
+0    < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 64240
+0    < R. 1:1(0) ack 1 win 0
